==English==
{{wikipedia}}
{{Webster 1913}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|NL.|en}} {{term|lang=la|rectum}}, abbreviation of {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|lang=la||rectum intestinum|the straight intestine}}, {{term|lang=la|rectum}}, neuter of {{term|lang=la|rectus||straight}}. See [[right]].

===Noun===
{{en-noun|recta|rectums}}

# {{context|anatomy|lang=en}} The [[terminal]] part of the large [[intestine]] through which feces pass.

====Derived terms====
* [[rectal]]

